<title>UK: UK Apr oil output down 44k bpd to 2.54 mln - WoodMa.</title>
<headline>UK Apr oil output down 44k bpd to 2.54 mln - WoodMa.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British oil production fell to 2.54 million barrels per day (bpd) in April from 2.58 million in March, consultants Wood Mackenzie said on Monday.</p>
<p>Output from the Brent field fell by 54,000 bpd to 115,000 bpd as a result of the shutdown of the Brent Delta platform as part of a long-term redevelopment programme.</p>
<p>Nelson, which feeds the Forties stream, also saw production fall to 138,000 bpd from 151,000 bpd as some wells were shut in to allow maintenance work to improve the quality of waste water.</p>
<p>Despite the fall, British oil output was still running 35,000 bpd above the levels of April last year.</p>
